---
layout: base.njk
title: "Example Tracks"
description: "Hand-composed example tracks in Perception Studio — drilling down into the exact DSP modules, routing topologies, and bus trees each composition exemplifies."
---

<section class="section grid-backdrop" style="border-top:0">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="prose-eyebrow"><a href="/learn/" style="text-decoration:none">← Learn</a> · Example Tracks</p>
      <h1>Example tracks</h1>
      <p class="prose-lead">
        Each example track is hand-composed to demonstrate specific synthesis modules, parallel
        outlet sends, and bus routing topologies inside Perception Studio.
      </p>
    </div>

    <article class="prose" style="margin-top:44px">
      <h2>1. Silt Relay — 138 BPM · 18 Bars</h2>
      <p>
        Demonstrates <strong>spectral morphing</strong>, <strong>16-voice granular synthesis</strong>,
        <strong>formant-preserving FFT pitch shifting</strong>, and <strong>parallel outlet sends</strong>
        into sidechained stereo buses.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>spectral</code> + <code>grainCloud</code> — <em>Throat / metal</em> runs a two-source spectral morph while <em>Spore wheel</em> drives a seeded granular cloud.</li>
        <li><code>shifter</code> + <code>modal</code> — <em>Glass pins</em> blends a formant-preserved perfect fifth at 22% wet into the <em>Pin bed</em> and <em>Objects</em> buses.</li>
        <li><code>split</code> / <code>delay</code> / <code>route</code> — <em>Rivet pulse</em> taps 6% of its stereo channel-swap outlet into the kick-keyed <em>Undertow</em> bus while feeding <em>Objects</em> dry and 19% to <em>Space</em>.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="gallery-grid" style="margin-top:24px; margin-bottom:64px">
      {% for shot in site.gallery.slice(0, 3) %}
      <article class="shot-card">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="shot-btn"
          data-lightbox-src="{{ shot.image }}"
          data-lightbox-alt="{{ shot.title }}"
          data-lightbox-title="{{ shot.title }}"
          data-lightbox-caption="{{ shot.caption }}"
        >
          <img src="{{ shot.image }}" alt="{{ shot.title }}" {% if loop.first %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %} decoding="async">
        </button>
        <div class="shot-meta">
          <span class="card-tag">{{ shot.tag }}</span>
          <h3>{{ shot.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ shot.caption }}</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2>2. Broken Circuitry: Reassembly — 97.5 BPM · 17 Tracks</h2>
      <p>
        Demonstrates <strong>multi-track arrangement</strong>, <strong>phase-distortion operators</strong>,
        <strong>nested stereo bus outputs</strong>, and <strong>mid-patch outlet taps</strong> across
        17 interleaved voices.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>operator</code> + <code>PatchInstrument</code> — detuned phase-distortion leads paired with custom waveguide and loss-filter patches.</li>
        <li><strong>Nested buses</strong> — <em>Keys bus</em> feeds into <em>pads</em> with live cycle detection and a 6.50 s <code>reverb</code> Space return.</li>
        <li><strong>Outlet taps</strong> — tap <em>Loss filter 3</em> straight into <em>pads</em> and <em>Keys bus</em> without altering the dry chain.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="gallery-grid" style="margin-top:24px">
      {% for shot in site.gallery.slice(3, 6) %}
      <article class="shot-card">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="shot-btn"
          data-lightbox-src="{{ shot.image }}"
          data-lightbox-alt="{{ shot.title }}"
          data-lightbox-title="{{ shot.title }}"
          data-lightbox-caption="{{ shot.caption }}"
        >
          <img src="{{ shot.image }}" alt="{{ shot.title }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </button>
        <div class="shot-meta">
          <span class="card-tag">{{ shot.tag }}</span>
          <h3>{{ shot.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ shot.caption }}</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
